{"step_index":1487,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T10:08:00Z","thinking":"Checking for existing jobs involves iterating through recent jobs on the server. The aim is to identify and retrieve job data if a matching filename is found, thereby avoiding redundant uploads and conserving API quota. A helper function will be used to encapsulate this logic.\n\n\nThe code attempts to locate and retrieve a completed job on the server by checking filenames and status.  If a completed job is found, it extracts job details using appropriate methods based on data structure presence. This retrieved data is then returned for processing. Any errors during job retrieval are handled by printing an error message.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import json\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unstructured_transform_client import TransformClient\n\ntest_pdf = Path(r\"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy\\جملة العمروووو.pdf\")\nsettings_path = Path(r\"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\settings.json\")\nwith open(settings_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    settings = json.load(f)\n\napi_key = settings[\"unstructured_api_key\"]\nclient = TransformClient(api_key=api_key, server_url=\"https://transform.unstructured.io\")\n\nschema = {\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n    \"title\": \"Supplier Product Names\",\n    \"description\": \"Extract product entries from all pages as source data only. Return one entry per source product row, preserving duplicates and different strengths. Include products even when price or quantity is blank or zero. Copy names faithfully without spelling repair or inferred digits. Do not infer stock, requested quantities or shortage matches.\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"description\": \"Every product entry from every page, in document order. Keep repeated entries. Exclude document headers, footers, contact details, column labels and totals.\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"item_name_raw\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Copy the complete product name/description exactly as present in the source, preserving Arabic, English, mixed text, spelling, strengths, units, dosage form, pack numbers, punctuation and manufacturer text. Do not correct, translate or complete it. Exclude values belonging to separate price, discount or quantity columns, but retain numbers written inside the name itself.\",\n                    },\n                    \"source_page\": {\n                        \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"],\n                        \"description\": \"The 1-based source page containing this product entry, taken from the source page metadata. Return null when unavailable; do not guess.\",\n                    },\n                },\n                \"required\": [\"item_name_raw\", \"source_page\"],\n                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n            },\n        },\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"items\"],\n    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n}\n\nprint(f\"[*] Step 1: Uploading test PDF: {test_pdf.name} ({test_pdf.stat().st_size} bytes)...\")\nt0 = time.time()\nwith open(test_pdf, \"rb\") as f:\n    result = client.extract.from_document(\n        input=f,\n        schema=schema,\n        wait_seconds=600\n    )\n\nif hasattr(result, 'model_dump'):\n    result_data = result.model_dump()\nelif hasattr(result, '__dict__'):\n    result_data = result.__dict__\nelse:\n    result_data = dict(result)\n\njob_id = result_data.get(\"id\")\nstatus = str(result_data.get(\"status\"))\nprint(f\"[*] Initial response: Job ID={job_id}, Status={status}, Elapsed={time.time()-t0:.1f}s\")\n\nif \"completed\" not in status.lower():\n    print(f\"[*] Polling job {job_id} until completed...\")\n    for i in range(60):\n        time.sleep(5)\n        job_res = client.jobs.get(job_id)\n        if hasattr(job_res, 'model_dump'):\n            job_data = job_res.model_dump()\n        else:\n            job_data = dict(job_res)\n        cur_status = str(job_data.get(\"status\"))\n        print(f\"    -> Status at {time.time()-t0:.1f}s: {cur_status}\")\n        if \"completed\" in cur_status.lower():\n            result_data = job_data\n            break\n        elif \"fail\" in cur_status.lower() or \"error\" in cur_status.lower():\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Job failed: {job_data}\")\n\n# Count extracted items\nextracted_data = result_data.get(\"extracted_data\", [])\nall_items = []\nfor block in extracted_data:\n    data = block.get(\"data\", {})\n    if isinstance(data, dict) and \"items\" in data:\n        for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n            if isinstance(item, dict) and item.get(\"item_name_raw\"):\n                all_items.append(item[\"item_name_raw\"])\n\nprint(f\"[+] Extraction complete! Total items extracted: {len(all_items)}\")\nprint(f\"[+] Sample items: {all_items[:5]}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n[*] Step 2: Testing smart remote lookup to verify re-upload avoidance...\")\nfound_job = None\nfor j in client.jobs.iterate():\n    source = getattr(j, \"source\", None)\n    fname = getattr(source, \"filename\", None) if source else None\n    st = str(getattr(j, \"status\", \"\")).lower()\n    if fname == test_pdf.name and \"completed\" in st:\n        found_job = j\n        break\n\nif found_job:\n    print(f\"[+] SUCCESS! Found existing completed job {found_job.id} for {test_pdf.name}\")\n    cached_job = client.jobs.get(found_job.id)\n    print(f\"[+] Retrieved data directly from server without re-upload!\")\nelse:\n    print(\"[-] Did not find job in iterate()\")\n\nprint(\"\\n[*] Step 3: Cleaning up test job from server...\")\nif job_id:\n    client.jobs.delete(job_id)\n    print(f\"[+] Cleaned up job {job_id}. Server is clean!\")\n","Description":"Comprehensive test script for Unstructured","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\test_pipeline.py","toolAction":"Write test pipeline","toolSummary":"Write test pipeline"}}]}
