{"step_index":1559,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T10:13:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T13:13:55+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T13:13:55+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///D:/miniconda3/envs/venv/Lib/site-packages/unstructured_transform_client/_multipart.py`\nTotal Lines: 101\nTotal Bytes: 4005\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"The multipart request openapi-generator refuses to emit.\n2: \n3: POST /api/v2/extract declares two request bodies in openapi.yaml:\n4: \n5:     application/json      -> ExtractRequest         (extract against a parse)\n6:     multipart/form-data   -> ExtractDocumentRequest (extract from a document)\n7: \n8: openapi-generator emits a method for the first and nothing for the second.\n9: `ExtractDocumentRequest` does not appear in the generated models at all, in\n10: either Python or TypeScript. There is no warning; the operation simply cannot\n11: be called that way from a generated client.\n12: \n13: So the request is assembled here — over the GENERATED transport, not a second\n14: HTTP stack. `param_serialize` applies the same auth, the same default headers,\n15: and the same serialization rules as every other call, and\n16: `response_deserialize` maps the response through the same generated models. A\n17: hand-rolled requests/httpx call would have had to reimplement all of that and\n18: would drift from it.\n19: \"\"\"\n20: \n21: from __future__ import annotations\n22: \n23: from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n24: \n25: if TYPE_CHECKING:\n26:     from ._client import TransformClient\n27: \n28: # EXACTLY the status codes openapi.yaml declares for POST /api/v2/extract, so\n29: # the JSON and multipart variants of one operation deserialize identically.\n30: #\n31: # Derived from the contract rather than guessed at: an earlier version invented\n32: # 403/422/502 (not declared here) while omitting 413 (declared) — so an\n33: # oversized document, the one error a large upload actually hits, fell through\n34: # to the generic path instead of deserializing as an Error.\n35: _RESPONSE_TYPES: dict[str, str] = {\n36:     \"200\": \"ParseResult\",\n37:     \"202\": \"JobAccepted\",\n38:     \"400\": \"Error\",\n39:     \"401\": \"Error\",\n40:     \"404\": \"Error\",\n41:     \"409\": \"Error\",\n42:     \"413\": \"Error\",\n43:     \"415\": \"Error\",\n44: }\n45: \n46: \n47: def post_multipart(\n48:     client: TransformClient,\n49:     *,\n50:     path: str,\n51:     file_field: str,\n52:     file_value: tuple[str, bytes] | None,\n53:     fields: dict[str, str | None],\n54:     wait_seconds: int | None = None,\n55: ) -> Any:\n56:     \"\"\"POST a multipart body and deserialize through the generated models.\"\"\"\n57:     api_client = client._api_client\n58: \n59:     # Mirrors what the generated multipart operations build. Getting any of\n60:     # these three wrong produces an EMPTY request body with no Content-Type\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":1560,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T10:13:55Z","thinking":"Document parsing occurs through a dedicated function, and the subsequent extraction of structured data utilizes another function that depends on the prior parsing stage. Examining the API further, extraction appears to necessitate the parse ID as input to the extraction function. This observation indicates a sequential process: document parsing followed by structured data extraction.\n\n\nThe provided code snippet confirms that the extraction process uses the `parse_id` obtained from the prior parsing stage.  It also highlights the use of a schema for specifying the desired extracted data and an iterative approach to process the results. This further reinforces the sequential execution pattern: parse then extract.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unstructured_transform_client import TransformClient\n\nsettings_path = Path(r\"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\settings.json\")\nwith open(settings_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    settings = json.load(f)\n\nclient = TransformClient(\n    api_key=settings[\"unstructured_api_key\"],\n    server_url=\"https://transform.unstructured.io\"\n)\n\ntest_pdf = Path(r\"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy\\جملة العمروووو.pdf\")\n\nschema = {\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n    \"title\": \"Supplier Product Names\",\n    \"description\": \"Extract product entries from all pages as source data only. Return one entry per source product row, preserving duplicates and different strengths. Include products even when price or quantity is blank or zero. Copy names faithfully without spelling repair or inferred digits. Do not infer stock, requested quantities or shortage matches.\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"description\": \"Every product entry from every page, in document order. Keep repeated entries. Exclude document headers, footers, contact details, column labels and totals.\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"item_name_raw\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Copy the complete product name/description exactly as present in the source, preserving Arabic, English, mixed text, spelling, strengths, units, dosage form, pack numbers, punctuation and manufacturer text. Do not correct, translate or complete it. Exclude values belonging to separate price, discount or quantity columns, but retain numbers written inside the name itself.\",\n                    },\n                    \"source_page\": {\n                        \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"],\n                        \"description\": \"The 1-based source page containing this product entry, taken from the source page metadata. Return null when unavailable; do not guess.\",\n                    },\n                },\n                \"required\": [\"item_name_raw\", \"source_page\"],\n                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n            },\n        },\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"items\"],\n    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n}\n\nprint(\"1. Parsing document with client.parse.run(document=f)...\")\nwith open(test_pdf, \"rb\") as f:\n    parsed = client.parse.run(document=f, wait_seconds=600)\n\nparse_id = parsed.id\nprint(\"Parse ID:\", parse_id, \"Status:\", getattr(parsed, \"status\", None))\n\nprint(\"2. Extracting with client.extract.run(parse_id=parse_id, schema=schema)...\")\next_result = client.extract.run(parse_id=parse_id, schema=schema, wait_seconds=600)\nprint(\"Extract result type:\", type(ext_result))\nprint(\"Extract result:\", ext_result)\n\nif hasattr(ext_result, \"extracted_data\"):\n    print(\"Found extracted_data! Length:\", len(ext_result.extracted_data))\n    for x in ext_result.extracted_data:\n        print(\"Item data:\", getattr(x, \"data\", None))\n","Description":"Test parse then extract","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\test_two_step.py","toolAction":"Test two-step extraction","toolSummary":"Test two-step extraction"}}]}
